Problem: Intersection in Y Shaped Lists
Link: https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/intersection-point-in-y-shapped-linked-lists/1

Problem Statement:

You are given the heads of two non-empty singly linked lists, head1 and head2, that intersect at a certain point. Return that Node where these two linked lists intersect.

Note: It is guaranteed that the intersected node always exists.

In the custom input you have to give input for CommonList which pointed at the end of both head1 and head2 to form a Y-shaped linked list.
Examples:

Input: head1: 10 -> 15 -> 30, head2: 3 -> 6 -> 9 -> 15 -> 30
Output: 15
Explanation: From the above image, it is clearly seen that the common part is 15 -> 30, whose starting point is 15.
    
Input: head1: 4 -> 1 -> 8 -> 5, head2: 5 -> 6 -> 1 -> 8 -> 5
Output: 1
Explanation: From the above image, it is clearly seen that the common part is 1 -> 8 -> 5, whose starting point is 1.
    
Constraints:
2 ≤ total number of nodes ≤ 2*10^5
-10^4 ≤ node->data ≤ 10^4

CODE:

/*
class Node {
public:
    int data;
    Node* next;

    Node(int x) {
        data = x;
        next = NULL;
    }
};
*/

class Solution {
  public:
    Node* intersectPoint(Node* head1, Node* head2) {
        //  Code Here
        
        //1st Approach: 
        //Using the logic of
        //Find the Start of Loop LL
        //i.e., reaching the end of list either using head1 or head2,
        //& connecting it back to where we started, either head1 or head2,
        //creating a loop within LL, & finding the start of the loop,
        //start of the loop == (POI) Point of Intersection in Y-Shaped LL.
        
        //2nd Approach:
        //Calculate totalNoOfNodes in each list1 & list2,
        //find the difference 
        //whichever is bigger, 
        //initiate that list with corresponding head + (above) difference,
        //Increment both the list by 1, their meeting point is POI.
        
        //It is guaranteed that the intersected node always exists
        
        int count1 = 0, count2 = 0;
        
        Node* curr1 = head1;
        Node* curr2 = head2;
        
        while(curr1) {
            count1++;
            curr1 = curr1->next;
        }
        
        while(curr2) {
            count2++;
            curr2 = curr2->next;
        }
        
        bool flag = 0;
        int diff = 0;
        
        if(count2>count1) {
            flag = 1;
        }
        
        curr1 = head1;
        curr2 = head2;
        
        //Finding the difference,
        //& whichever list is bigger, 
        //skipping the differnce no of nodes.
        
        if(flag) {
            diff = count2-count1;
            while(diff) {
                curr2 = curr2->next;
                diff--;
            }
        } else {
            diff = count1-count2;
            while(diff) {
                curr1 = curr1->next;
                diff--;
            }
        }
        
        while(curr1!=curr2) {
            curr1 = curr1->next;
            curr2 = curr2->next;
        }
        
        
        //We reach POI, curr1 == curr2,
        return curr1;
        
        
    }
};
